"""Collision part 2: sphere sweeps, slides, body sweeps (game/collision_sweep.cpp, collision_body.cpp)

Run: set MUT_HARNESS=collision, MUT_DEFS=-DCOLLISION_QUICK, MUT_EXTRA_SRCS=ls3df/src/math/math.cpp,
MUT_EXTRA_INC=ls3df/src, then python _re/harness/mutrun.py _re/harness/collision/mutations/mutate_collision2.py WORK
[JOBS]. Needs the levels (MISSIONS_DIR) and the original executable (HD2_ORIGINAL_EXE, HD2_GAME_DIR: without it
most of part 2 has nothing to compare with). Labels: S collision_sweep.cpp, B collision_body.cpp, + line.
Generated by _re/harness/shots/gen_mutations.py per source (lines unique in their file), merged.

Result (2026-11-11): 736 mutants; 534 killed, 71 not building, 131 survived (S 547 and S 549 are killed by
sweep_diff.cpp, which mutrun does not run: 129 survive both).
- 76 comparisons at their boundary (< for <=, ...): the same unless a value equals the limit exactly, which the
  random sweeps do not produce (B 274: one more sphere reset, never read).
- initial values and array sizes always overwritten or not read: S 24, 29-32, 34, 35, 41 (the sweep's fields, the
  distance global), S 172, 183, 184, 188, 203, 217, 513, 514, 516 (array sizes), S 314 (t, set on both paths);
  B 47 del / num with B 50 del (the wall's y is zeroed twice), B 119 / 120 (read only with a contact), B 228 (a
  normal's fourth word), B 309-311 (overwritten, or tested >= 0), B 348 (3 walls act as 2), B 363 (del, num,
  arith) / B 365 (overwritten by the ground contact after), B 316 / 386 arith (bodies have a sphere at least);
- within the comparisons' tolerance (0.001 -> 0.0015): B 231 num, B 275, B 360;
- the same with any input: S 138 (a negative distance is only compared as below every contact), S 923 (the length
  is not read again after a volume), S 930 / 931 (the fallback side scaled: the slab and the triangles' extents
  scale alike), S 732-735 (num, arith: the volume cells' ranges one cell wider or narrower, within the grid's own
  margin);
- not reached: S 385 (a hull primitive started inside, its stored center: my hulls' are 0), S 567 (a rectangle's
  corner bit for z), B 231 arith (the step up from the top sphere meeting something above: the shift's sign),
  B 276 / 279 (the low sweep starting again after meeting a human when contacts were already recorded), B 334 (the
  wall across the way counted twice: my wedges give two walls either way).
Runs: 168 survived the first. Added from them: harder body places (a V of 62-degree slopes, a slot narrower than a
body, a roof and an overhang, standing humans by the walls, feet below and above surfaces, moves going up),
different radii on a body's spheres, a contact table not zero before the move, MoveSpheres in every place (the
places and the sweeps went by i % 3 together, so each sweep saw one kind of place), upward vertical sweeps.
A lesson: the slides' and bodies' excuse "the port's steps over the original's sweeps give the original's" used my
own copy of the steps, so it proved the copy, not the port: B 81 / 82 (MoveSpheres keeping the nearest contact)
survived three runs behind it. The copy must now also give the port's result over the port's sweeps; they died.
The original executable decides throughout: SphereTest, SlideSphere and the body sweeps are called in it on the
same world (original_exe.h). It found one port bug before the mutation runs: MoveSpheresLow's iteration cap after
meeting a human is one lower in the original (0x0071cf4e), fixed.
"""
